1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,990
One processor will blink lights, print a counter and read a touch pad, all appearing

2
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:09,780
to run together. We'll read every line of the lesson file.

3
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:16,617
Create your project with the touch driver ticked. Paste main.c and the pin file.

4
00:00:16,617 --> 00:00:19,900
Then copy the three engine files into source.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,000
Spell the last one with a capital S. Don't edit them.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:34,812
Important. In the second half, follow step numbers, not position. Five, six, seven,

7
00:00:34,812 --> 00:00:43,560
eight, nine, ten. Step seven sits at the bottom, because it never returns.

8
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:54,899
Line 88 brings memory tools. Lines 89 to 93: board, pins, clock, text and pins on

9
00:00:54,899 --> 00:00:55,920
and off.

10
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:59,940
Line 94 is the touch driver.

11
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:06,440
Line 95 is our scheduler. It gives us two functions and a millisecond counter.

12
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:12,640
Switch on lines 127 to 132 with the comment shortcut.

13
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:18,420
Line 127 declares a task: a function with nothing in and nothing out.

14
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:26,103
Line 129, for with two semicolons, means repeat forever. The empty brackets do

15
00:01:26,103 --> 00:01:26,840
nothing.

16
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:30,140
May a task ever return?

17
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:35,640
Your turn. Pause the video.

18
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:38,600
No. There is nobody to return to.

19
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,720
Switch on lines 173 to 201.

20
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:46,500
Line 175 makes a pin settings form.

21
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:56,200
Lines 176 and 177 remember when each light last switched, starting at zero.

22
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:03,260
Lines 179 and 180: outputs that start at one, which means off.

23
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:10,240
Lines 182 and 183 apply the form to the red pin, then the blue pin.

24
00:02:11,240 --> 00:02:14,360
Line 185 starts the endless loop.

25
00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:20,060
Line 187 reads the clock: milliseconds since the scheduler started.

26
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:27,440
Line 189 asks whether 250 milliseconds have passed since the red light changed.

27
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:33,940
If so, line 191 flips red, and line 192 writes down the time.

28
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:40,760
Lines 195 to 199 do the same for blue every 80 milliseconds.

29
00:02:41,260 --> 00:02:45,020
Why greater than or equal, and not exactly equal?

30
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:50,520
Your turn. Pause the video.

31
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:53,800
If the task is paused, it could miss the exact moment.

32
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:57,280
Switch on lines 233 to 251.

33
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:03,060
Lines 235 and 236: the last print time and a private count.

34
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:09,320
Line 240 reads the clock. Line 242 waits for 300 milliseconds to pass.

35
00:03:09,820 --> 00:03:16,380
Line 244 adds one. Line 246 prints the time and the count.

36
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,680
Line 248 remembers when we printed.

37
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:23,960
Switch on lines 285 to 324.

38
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:32,700
Lines 287 to 289: touch settings, the untouched baseline, and the last sample time.

39
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:37,360
Lines 291 to 293 start the touch hardware.

40
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:45,904
Lines 295 and 296 clear the box and measure the baseline. Keep fingers off at

41
00:03:45,904 --> 00:03:46,740
startup.

42
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:50,700
Line 302: every 400 milliseconds.

43
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:56,080
Lines 307 and 308 choose pad one and start a scan.

44
00:03:56,580 --> 00:04:00,740
Lines 310 to 312 wait for the scan to finish.

45
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:05,800
Lines 314 and 315 read the count and clear the flag.

46
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:13,660
Line 317 subtracts the baseline, so zero means untouched. Line 319 prints it.

47
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:16,720
Line 321 remembers the time.

48
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:23,802
Now inside main. Switch on lines 358 to 364. They wake the board and print a title

49
00:04:23,802 --> 00:04:24,840
and a warning.

50
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:30,000
Switch on lines 396 to 398.

51
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:35,700
Each line adds a task: slot number, a name, and the function to run.

52
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:41,560
All three slots get the idle task. An empty slot would crash the board.

53
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:46,640
Go to the bottom. Switch on lines 512 to 516.

54
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:53,780
Line 512 starts the scheduler. It never returns. The loop after it is never reached.

55
00:04:54,280 --> 00:05:01,476
Build and load. You'll see the title, then silence. Three idle tasks are taking

56
00:05:01,476 --> 00:05:03,480
turns. That's success.

57
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:10,530
Go back up and switch on line 427. It replaces the idle task in slot zero with the

58
00:05:10,530 --> 00:05:11,120
blinker.

59
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:15,380
Load it. Expect blue to blink quickly and red slowly.

60
00:05:16,380 --> 00:05:20,460
Switch on line 454: the counter takes slot one.

61
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:26,477
Switch on line 480: the touch reader takes slot two. Keep your fingers off as it

62
00:05:26,477 --> 00:05:26,960
starts.

63
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:32,952
Both kinds of line appear while the lights blink. Touch pad one and watch delta

64
00:05:32,952 --> 00:05:33,300
rise.

65
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:38,520
An occasional jumbled line happens because two tasks share one text line.

66
00:05:39,520 --> 00:05:49,200
On line 189, change 250 to 1000. What happens to the red light?

67
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:54,700
Your turn. Pause the video.

68
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:57,100
It blinks four times more slowly.

69
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:06,121
On line 242, try 100. The counter prints three times as often, while the lights keep

70
00:06:06,121 --> 00:06:07,440
their rhythm.

71
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:13,140
You've used a scheduler and can explain every line of your tasks. Brilliant work.

